From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BananaDS <bananads@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] BananaDS: the in-game menu's LAN multiplayer page

Quick settings > LAN multiplayer (builds with BANANADS_LAN): Mode Off / Host / Join; Players, 2-16 (4 by
default), for a host while nobody else is in its session; Hosts found, a scrolling list like Cheats' with each
host's name, players and address, A joins one and the page says "Connecting..." meanwhile (up to 5 s) or why it
failed; the session's players with their ping; and Disconnect (a host's session ends; a joined player goes back
to looking for hosts). The menu polls the frontend twice a second and never waits for the network: the
emulator's thread does the work (Emu::lan_request). The mode changes without a restart while no local wireless
game is on; during one only Disconnect works, after a question, and the game keeps running behind the menu as
before. The choice is kept in bananads.conf (wifi.local off/host/join, wifi.local_players);
BANANADS_WIFI_LOCAL(_PLAYERS) in the environment still win at each start, and the page says so while one is
set. The player name shown is the DS name (BananaOS: Settings > Nintendo DS > DS name, firmware.nickname). The
modes are an enum the menu cycles through, so another (an automatic one) can be added after Join.
